WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.096 --> 00:00:02.596
(piano music)

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:08.083
- I grew up Mormon.

00:00:09.101 --> 00:00:11.733
(speaks foreign language)

00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:15.238
I was Mormon most of my life,
up until a few years ago.

00:00:15.238 --> 00:00:16.071
- Hi.

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:22.010
- I then left the Mormon Church,
and that is a whole story

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.620
that I want to talk about
today with all of you.

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.690
My purpose in doing this
is to share my perspective

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:31.170
so that anyone who is in
a situation like I was

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:34.000
a couple of years ago, who
is questioning and wondering

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.740
can have another perspective to lean on.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:38.950
I'm not looking to get into debates

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:43.950
or to talk about the history
or the theology of the church.

00:00:43.965 --> 00:00:45.670
I'll do that in future videos.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.050
Today, all I want to do
is tell you the story

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:52.019
of how and why I left the Mormon Church.

00:00:52.019 --> 00:00:52.947
23rd of May, 2000, 2009.

00:01:00.173 --> 00:01:02.070
What are we even doing out here, man?

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:03.430
I grew up Mormon.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:07.750
Both my parents were Mormon
or LDS, Latter-day Saints.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:10.290
I grew up going to Mormon youth camp.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:13.120
I then eventually served
a two-year mission

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:18.120
in Tijuana, Mexico, where
for two years, I went around

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.370
and spoke to people in
Spanish about the church

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:25.178
and learned a lot, learned
to speak Spanish fluently.

00:01:25.178 --> 00:01:26.880
(man speaks foreign language)

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.255
- [Man] How you feel?

00:01:28.255 --> 00:01:29.934
(speaks foreign language)

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:30.767
(man laughs)

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:32.970
(speaks Spanish)

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:35.770
I then went to the Mormon university

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:37.940
called Brigham Young
University in Provo, Utah,

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:39.060
where I graduated.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:43.600
I went through all Mormon
rituals in the church and temple.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.930
I worked in the temple as
a volunteer for a time.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:50.880
I was very, very Mormon,
and I believed it.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.130
I believed deeply in the unique doctrine

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.450
of the church of Jesus
Christ of Latter-day Saints,

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.750
which is a Christian organization

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:01.778
unlike any other Christian
organization in its doctrine.

00:02:01.778 --> 00:02:04.611
(heartfelt music)

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:09.390
The story of how I decided to leave this

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:12.333
really begins with the birth of my son.

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:19.390
Isabelle, who also grew up Mormon,

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:21.390
and I got married in the temple,

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:23.600
which is a huge Mormon ritual.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.590
It's a huge part of being in the church.

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:27.660
We got married in the temple.

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.150
We went back to BYU together,

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:33.430
and a few weeks before
we graduated from BYU,

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:35.950
we had a baby, or Ize had a baby.

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:37.110
I didn't have a baby.

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:38.500
She had a baby.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.760
Then we took finals and graduated, like,

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.720
literally two weeks later.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.870
Here we are literally in our cap and gown

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:47.230
with Henry, who is, like, two weeks old.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:51.053
After we graduated, we
moved out to Washington, DC,

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:54.890
and that's when my wheels
really started to turn.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:57.420
I started to think, you
know, I have a child now.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:59.570
I have to decide how I raise this child

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:01.420
and what I teach him about the world.

00:03:02.331 --> 00:03:04.760
(rolls tongue)

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.510
Da, da, da, da, da.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:09.360
I think having Henry really made me wonder

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:12.690
and think about how I should
teach him about the world.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:17.450
I'd grown up with this firm
conviction of the LDS doctrine

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.160
and its beliefs about the world,

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:23.050
which are very specific and very peculiar.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:25.860
And I really started to question,

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:27.180
is this what I want to teach my son?

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.900
And the answer initially was yes.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:33.170
I want to teach him everything
that I know about this faith

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:34.620
because I really believed it.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.470
So, we're moving out to Washington, DC,

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:39.270
and I realized that if I'm
gonna teach this to my son,

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:42.490
I need to double down on my faith.

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:44.650
I need to go deeper than I ever have

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:47.730
and really, really establish
a strong foundation

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.860
and conviction around this doctrine.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.990
I had one, but I knew
it needed to be stronger

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:53.187
if I was gonna teach my son this.

00:03:53.187 --> 00:03:56.580
One of the things I loved about
Mormon doctrine at the time

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:00.810
was that there was always a
push to ask God if it was true.

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.930
Not to trust any people
or any organization,

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:07.790
but to, like, get on your knees
and say, God, is this true?

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:09.470
Is this church actually real?

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:14.280
Is all of the things that they
say actually the real deal?

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.970
I had kind of taken advantage
of that promise before,

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:17.960
but never really.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:21.000
I'd always been in a setting of pressure,

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:26.000
whether it was my home as
a kid or my mission or BYU.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:30.090
In other words, there was
always an incentive to believe.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:31.770
So I'd never really been in a situation

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:34.480
where I could truly ask this question

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:37.110
and not feel like there
was some price to pay

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.850
if I decided I didn't believe.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:42.360
Being in Washington DC
with my child out on my own

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.740
in the workforce was my opportunity,

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.530
so I spent an entire year

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:48.953
reading the "Book of
Mormon", going to church.

00:04:48.953 --> 00:04:50.910
I had a responsibility at church

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:53.190
that I was putting a lot of work into,

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:56.730
and praying every morning and every night

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.680
for some sort of conviction.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.810
I said, I am more earnest and sincere

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.430
than I've ever been about this.

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:05.340
I'm willing to listen to any answer.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.200
I just need an answer.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.600
I spent a year doing this.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:09.433
A year.

00:05:09.433 --> 00:05:10.520
That's a long time.

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:12.150
And then I remember this day,

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:15.473
I was biking into Washington, DC,

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:19.200
on a sunny, like, spring day,

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:23.290
and it just hit me in
some really strong way

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:27.870
that no, this isn't working.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:30.360
I've put in the years of asking

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:34.770
and the effort towards
(sighs) making this work,

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.950
and it wasn't working.

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.863
This isn't true for me.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:45.050
And like a switch, it just
so much came out of me,

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:49.850
and I quickly decided that I was done.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:50.890
I don't think it was all at once.

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:53.440
I think I had been slowly
moving in this direction

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:57.450
for a long time, but
in a moment of clarity,

00:05:57.450 --> 00:06:00.210
it clicked for me in a
very satisfying and, like,

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.240
very true way.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:05.000
So Iz, who, Ize, Isabelle,

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.130
whatever you want to call her, my wife,

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:08.060
it didn't click for her.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:10.400
She was not on this journey that I was on.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.020
And I came back and I told her.

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:14.480
I said, I think I am done being Mormon.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:15.570
And I had always been the sort

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:18.480
of more devout, convicted Mormon.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.707
And she was just like, "What?

00:06:20.707 --> 00:06:22.857
"Like, you just, like, have decided

00:06:22.857 --> 00:06:25.927
"to be out of this church?"
And she full on said, like,

00:06:25.927 --> 00:06:27.517
"This is gonna end our marriage.

00:06:27.517 --> 00:06:30.290
"Like, you can't just leave the church."

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:31.123
And I just told her.

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:33.210
I said, "This is where I stand
and this is what I feel,"

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:35.460
and I felt very strongly about it.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:39.020
Luckily, soon enough,
Ize was on her own path

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:42.540
of reconciling her
thoughts about the church,

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.380
her qualms with the church,

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:47.330
and soon she would join me in this path

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:48.610
towards leaving the church.

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:51.930
Now, I call it a path because
that's exactly what it is.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:55.690
Leaving any Orthodox religion is not easy.

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:58.370
There are layers and
layers of psychological

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:01.900
and cultural conditioning
that you don't even realize

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:04.350
is there until you start to peel it back.

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:06.880
So, even though we started
to leave the church,

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:10.050
we were still going to
church every Sunday,

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:11.650
which I don't really
understand in retrospect.

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:13.940
All I can say is that, like, we were just,

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:15.000
that's what we did every Sunday.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:15.833
We went to church,

00:07:15.833 --> 00:07:17.410
and there was some guilt
if we didn't go to church,

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:19.420
and so we went to church.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:22.750
But we slowly started to
feel an emptiness towards it,

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.240
and over the course of six months,

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:28.730
we finally decided to
stop going to church.

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:31.630
My behavior didn't change all of a sudden.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:33.140
Like, I didn't leave the church

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:36.840
so I could start drinking
alcohol or coffee or smoking.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.590
Like, that was not a part
of the agenda for me.

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:42.630
I kind of just carried on
exactly how I'd always been,

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:44.980
except for now I looked
around in the world

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:48.600
and I didn't have a doctrinal
theological framework

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:52.310
to understand it, which
was at once exhilarating

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:54.540
and horrifying at the same time.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:57.820
My existential view had
been so neatly packaged

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:59.680
by the plan of salvation,

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.240
which is at the key doctrinal framework

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:04.040
within the Mormon Church,
and that was now gone.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:04.990
I had no plan.

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:08.010
I had no framework to
make sense of the world.

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:11.220
Exhilarating, but horrifying.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:13.340
There was also a deep fear

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:17.980
of the cultural and social
repercussions of my decision.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:21.890
Most of my friends were
still LDS or Mormon,

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:23.940
and, of course, my family was, too.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:26.540
So was Ize's. And let me just
try to give you a perspective

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:28.670
on why this is such a big deal.

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:30.980
A quick primmer on Mormon theology

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:32.750
is that our whole purpose in life

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:36.810
is to come down here to
Earth to learn and to grow

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:38.830
and to progress and to attain knowledge,

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:43.830
and to fulfill certain we call
them covenants or rituals.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:47.470
There are four of them
that are really important

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:51.190
to do while you're on Earth,
baptism, confirmation,

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:53.840
this hour-long ritual inside the temple,

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:56.050
and then, called the endowment,

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.760
and then the ceiling or marriage.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:00.450
If you can do those four things,

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:01.810
then you're in really good shape.

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.080
You have the knowledge necessary

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:06.370
to go back and live in
the top tier of heaven.

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:08.070
And yes, in Mormon theology,

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:10.920
there are multiple tiers of heaven.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:12.450
If you're not able to
get these rituals done

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:15.320
while you're on Earth, no worries.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.530
When you're in the next
life, people on Earth

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.820
can do all of the rituals
for you when you're dead,

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:22.800
and then you can have those,

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:26.330
the chance to accept those
rituals or those covenants

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.250
when you're on the other side.

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:29.440
It's a huge deal.

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:31.490
I had gone through all of the rituals.

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:33.700
I had accepted all of those covenants,

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:35.150
which are very serious covenants.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:39.060
You wear undergarments that are symbolic

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:41.163
of those covenants that you've made.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:44.700
People call them, like,
secret underwear or whatever,

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.950
but it was just religious clothing

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:50.220
that symbolizes your
commitment to these doctrines.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:52.420
And the beauty of all of
this within Mormon doctrine

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:55.060
is if you do this and everyone
in your family does this,

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:57.780
then all of you are sealed together

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:01.700
in this never ending
chain of eternal family

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:04.360
that is at the epicenter
of Mormon doctrine.

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:05.270
If you know Mormons

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:07.190
and you know that they
are family-centered,

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:08.840
it's because of this.

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:12.520
The whole doctrine is based
on creating family units

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:15.800
that are all tied into this covenant,

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:19.010
these promises that bind
you, that seal you together

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:21.100
for time and all eternity.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:24.340
If you've accepted those
covenants, and then you leave,

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:26.900
you break away, you
reject those covenants,

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:30.013
you take off your garments,
you say I'm done with this,

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:36.173
that's a pretty big deal
within the LDS framework.

00:10:36.173 --> 00:10:39.360
You are no longer able
to be with your family

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:43.410
in the celestial glory of
the top tier of heaven.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.570
So if you believe that,
and you're a parent,

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:48.610
and you see your child
rejecting those covenants,

00:10:48.610 --> 00:10:51.110
rejecting that eternal
ceiling to the family,

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:54.220
you're basically seeing
your child go away,

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:57.460
and you feel like you're losing them.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:00.450
So unsurprisingly, people
leaving the Mormon Church

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:03.890
creates huge upset within families,

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.300
like many other religions.

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:08.430
It's not just an insular
cultural experience.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:13.010
It is a deeply held
doctrinal theological belief

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:16.770
that if you leave the church,
there are major consequences.

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:21.770
Luckily, I had parents who,
by the time I told them

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:26.920
that I was leaving the church,
were very open and loving

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:29.070
and accepting of my decision.

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:30.870
Certainly, it was hurtful for them,

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:32.960
but they did not project that onto me

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:35.540
in any way that made me feel ostracized.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:38.770
Unfortunately, that is not the
case for a lot of my friends

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:40.940
and a lot of other people
who have left the church.

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:44.550
But even still, with
parents who were accepting

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:49.550
and loving despite my decision,
I still had years of purging

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:53.520
and processing to do,
something that continues

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:57.360
to this day now four or five years later.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:00.490
What I didn't realize is
that I had internalized

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:05.040
a lot of assumptions of shame and guilt

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:09.590
and fear and judgment that
I didn't even realize I had.

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:13.240
And for the years following
leaving the church,

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:16.650
it was a process of slowly purging

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:19.290
and peeling back and
processing those things.

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:21.200
I went through the Mister Nice Guy phase,

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:22.660
which is a very common thing for people

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:24.510
who leave the LDS church, which is like,

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:27.220
I'm just leaving the
church nice and peaceful.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.590
I'm gonna not be mean.

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:30.500
I'm not gonna be spiteful
towards the church

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.860
because in the church, when you're in it,

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:36.080
there's sort of this, like, archetype

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:40.030
of the spiteful, angry
anti-Mormon who goes out

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.610
and spreads lies about the church,

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:43.890
and they're just offended and angry.

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:45.760
And I didn't want to be that person.

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:47.330
I don't want to be that archetype.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:48.960
And so I tried to maintain

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:51.500
very cordial relationships with everybody.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:52.930
I tried to be super nice.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:54.680
Like, you know, the church
was really great for me

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:57.020
and yet I just, you
know, disagreed with it,

00:12:57.020 --> 00:12:57.930
so I walked away.

00:12:57.930 --> 00:13:00.680
I went through that phase
for a couple of years.

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:02.200
But through therapy

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:04.440
and through a lot of thinking about this,

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:07.620
I came to understand that I actually had

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:11.640
some deep problems and
anger towards the church

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.160
and what it instilled in me.

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:14.900
I had anger and resentment

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:17.690
towards a lot of the authority structures

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:20.600
that made me feel unclean or dirty.

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:23.420
I had anger towards the
systems that made me feel

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:25.720
like obedience was the
most important thing,

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:29.430
that submission to a law from
God was much more important

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:33.270
than self-expression
and self-actualization.

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:36.330
I developed a resentment
towards the church structure

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:40.260
that has very homophobic
and heteronormative

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:42.480
and misogynistic structures

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.740
that taught me to think in those terms.

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:47.500
A church that purports to love everybody,

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:52.080
but deeply condemns certain
people because of who they love.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:55.550
I had to rewire so much
of that upon leaving,

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:57.410
and perhaps most frustratingly,

00:13:57.410 --> 00:14:01.660
and maybe this is gonna be hard
to communicate the nuance to

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:03.040
to someone who's not LDS,

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:07.350
but I felt deep frustration
at the church's claim

00:14:07.350 --> 00:14:10.540
to have a monopoly over
the fullness of truth,

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:14.710
that the few million
members are the only keepers

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:18.280
of the real truth of what
God wants today for us,

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:19.998
and that everyone else has truth, too,

00:14:19.998 --> 00:14:24.998
but through prophets and apostles
and modern day revelation,

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:29.060
the Mormons are actually the
ones who have the full picture.

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:30.250
They know what's going on.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:32.680
I believed that they had the truth

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.010
that was going to deliver me and my family

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:38.160
to eternal bliss in celestial glory.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:41.940
I believed that, and I
modeled my life around it

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:43.650
deep into my adulthood.

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:46.170
And I feel resentment that I did that,

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:48.840
and that the stakes were
so high for leaving,

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:52.250
for expressing myself and
my qualms for this doctrine.

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:54.300
Because after all, if you question it,

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:57.718
you're questioning prophets,
people who are talking to God.

00:14:57.718 --> 00:14:59.150
You can't do that.

00:14:59.150 --> 00:15:01.820
It all left me very confused

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:05.820
and required a lot of
healing and processing,

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:09.340
and that is still going on.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:10.720
And let me just be clear about something.

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.690
This isn't my millennial brain

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:15.140
trying to reject authority structures

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:18.770
and subvert old institutions
like is happening

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:20.600
in a lot of religious contexts right now.

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:22.090
A lot of people are leaving religion.

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:25.430
I wasn't trying to get away
from some disciplined structure.

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:27.510
My life is still a disciplined structure.

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:29.950
I still have a lot of the artifacts

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:31.470
from my Mormon upbringing.

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:34.500
What I was fleeing when
I left the Mormon Church

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:39.500
was a structure that I feel
like put down who I really was,

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:44.240
made me cover it up in the
name of a broader vision

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:48.520
of what righteousness is and
what Jesus wants me to do.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:49.790
It wasn't me.

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:51.390
It was harmful towards me,

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:53.410
and it was harmful towards others.

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:57.180
And the consequences were
severe if you spoke up

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:59.850
and you challenged the status quo.

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:02.500
The culture is not one
of discourse and debate.

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:04.580
It's one of obedience,

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:07.060
obedience, obedience, obedience.

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:10.250
Obedience is a hallmark belief

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:13.380
and tenet of the LDS experience,

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:16.370
and as a member, you feel it.

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:21.030
Leaving the church is
painful socially, mentally.

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:23.680
You experience a cost for doing so.

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:25.680
And if you're in that situation now,

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:28.300
which I know some of those watching are,

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:32.260
where you know that your
family and your peers

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:36.003
will think differently of
you if you decide to leave,

00:16:37.090 --> 00:16:39.840
just know that it's a lot
better on the other side,

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:41.540
if you choose yourself

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:44.690
and you choose your personal experience

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:47.930
and your personal expression,
and you honor that,

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:50.750
as opposed to honoring
the fear of obedience.

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:53.100
There's some years of pain and adjustment,

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:56.470
but there is a sense of
freedom on the other side.

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:57.870
This is uncomfortable for me to say.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.360
Even right now, I'm imagining

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:02.720
whether it's family or friends

00:17:02.720 --> 00:17:05.880
who are still active believers
in the church watching this.

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:09.500
I can feel that discomfort,
even now, years later,

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:13.316
of what are they thinking
of me making this video

00:17:13.316 --> 00:17:16.860
and effectively talking to
others who might be in the church

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:18.457
and telling them to leave.

00:17:18.457 --> 00:17:21.480
That old archetype of the bitter ex-Mormon

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:26.480
who's polarizing and extremist
is ringing in my ears.

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:31.410
And yet, day by day, those
voices and those old models,

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:35.410
they dissolve more and more,
and they become less loud

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:37.340
and they become less part of my identity.

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:39.510
I, for many years, did identify as someone

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:42.480
who used to be Mormon and now I'm not,

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:45.010
but yet, with time I'm slowly developing

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:47.408
my own new identity that isn't pinned

00:17:47.408 --> 00:17:51.240
to my reactionary
experience with the church,

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:54.130
but is just pinned to
who I am, what I love.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:56.030
I'm a father who loves my children.

00:17:56.030 --> 00:17:58.030
I love to learn about the world

00:17:58.030 --> 00:17:59.950
and explore and explain things.

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:01.990
I love film, I love animation.

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:04.710
I love moss, I love cooking.

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:08.640
I love reading stories to my boys

00:18:08.640 --> 00:18:10.350
and teaching them about the world.

00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:11.410
I love traveling.

00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:13.120
I love trains.

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:14.690
I love science.

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:19.010
I love the beauty of our world
and the mystery that it is

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:21.810
and the mystery of life and cultures.

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:25.100
That appreciation is enough for me.

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:28.500
I don't have a spiritual
framework to fill the vacuum.

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:30.290
I haven't joined some religion.

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.520
Maybe someday I will.

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:33.750
Maybe I will develop that, but for now,

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:37.470
the wonder of the world,
outside of the plan of salvation

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:40.490
and God looking out over his children

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:43.180
for this big plan of obedience,

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:45.940
outside of that, I feel
like there is plenty

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:48.960
to stand in awe of and love

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:53.960
without a God and a savior
to create meaning for me.

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:57.660
And yet, there's a strange
paradox within all of this

00:18:57.660 --> 00:18:59.250
that I have to talk about,

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:04.250
which is the Mormon experience
also gave me so much.

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:10.120
My mission, while I feel
conflicted about what I was doing

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:13.430
and how I was doing it,
I learned to work hard.

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:15.160
I learned to speak Spanish.

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:18.220
I learned to navigate
in cultural experiences

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:19.870
outside of my own.

00:19:19.870 --> 00:19:21.620
I was in Tijuana for two years

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:23.710
next to a giant international border,

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:26.470
one of the most violent and
intense borders on Earth,

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:30.340
and that instilled a love for the stories

00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:31.870
of people who live near borders,

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:34.680
which helped create my career.

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:37.690
My parents raising me in that environment

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:41.660
gave me beautiful
experiences and community,

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:44.140
taught me how to be industrious

00:19:44.140 --> 00:19:46.680
and hardworking and disciplined.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:50.620
It taught me how to care
and love and serve others.

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:52.770
Those are all good things.

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:55.480
So how do I reconcile the pain

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:59.190
and the psychological confusion

00:19:59.190 --> 00:20:02.160
that this organization brought to my life,

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:04.610
packaged tightly with the reality

00:20:04.610 --> 00:20:08.320
of all of the beautiful things
that it brought to my life?

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:11.840
The good, the community, the memories,

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:15.000
the values of honesty
and service and love?

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:19.280
That's a paradox that will
probably be with me forever.

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:23.380
It's impossible to summarize
this experience as one thing.

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:27.050
good or bad, and that's okay.

00:20:27.050 --> 00:20:28.430
That dissonance is okay.

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:32.850
So, that's a little bit of
my story and my thoughts

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:35.050
around why I left the Mormon Church.

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:36.220
I wanna hear from you,

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:38.890
especially those who
have experience with this

00:20:38.890 --> 00:20:41.170
and can speak about the complexities.

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:43.866
I also wanna hear from
those who have questions

00:20:43.866 --> 00:20:46.240
and are worried or scared.

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:48.060
This isn't an easy decision.

00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:49.470
I also want to hear from those

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:51.220
who have experience with this,

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:52.470
whether it's from the Mormon Church

00:20:52.470 --> 00:20:57.470
or any other Orthodox
insular religion or culture.

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:00.025
Breaking out of those systems is hard

00:21:00.025 --> 00:21:04.470
and sometimes not worth
it, but sometimes it is.

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:05.540
Sometimes it's worth it.

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:09.373
And sometimes on the other
side of that hard journey,

00:21:09.373 --> 00:21:12.043
there is a much brighter future.

